1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,740
This rock weighs 100 tons.

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,120
His job? Move it.

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,260
No crane.

4
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,200
He pushes.

5
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,260
The rock doesn't even notice.

6
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,480
So he ties a rope and pulls.

7
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,540
That rope is rated for 2 tons.

8
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,900
The rock weighs 50 times more.

9
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:14,880
Snap.

10
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:16,260
So he grabs a lever.

11
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,840
Long side, short side.

12
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:18,900
50 to 1.

13
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:19,780
He's too light,

14
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,900
so he adds a ton of sandbags.

15
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,180
And the edge lifts.

16
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,760
Now slide rollers underneath.

17
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,720
He's not dragging 100 tons anymore.

18
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,720
He's rolling it.

19
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:29,920
That only takes about 2 tons of pull.

20
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,280
A pry bar nudges it

21
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,620
a few centimeters per heave.

22
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,680
At this rate, it'll take a week.

23
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:36,140
So he builds a capstan.

24
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,820
Long arms, skinny drum.

25
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,820
20 to 1.

26
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,740
Loop the rope around a pulley on the rock,

27
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:41,680
and that doubles it.

28
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:42,620
One engineer,

29
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,980
40 times stronger.

30
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,980
The rollers move at half the rock's speed,

31
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,720
so it just keeps coming.

32
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:48,740
Destination reached.

33
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,300
One guy, one rock,

34
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:51,800
zero cranes.

35
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:54,220
Then the client texts.

